READING
  Odd n: doubling is an automorphism of the AP unit-clock sheaf. Even n: it is a boundary morphism from units to nonunits.
  At n=14 every unit witness doubles into gcd-2 residue; each image has one unit lift and one nonunit lift, exposing the 2-block seam.
  Dihedral VT point-sets glue local vertex profiles with either trivial cyclic monodromy or a two-block bracelet monodromy.
  Rooted tournament quotients show the sheaf warning: source is rigid, but fixed-root, parent, and orbit-size labels become mixed once cross fibers are forgotten.
